 ### Free/Busy Service (Read-Optimized)
 
-**Responsibility**: Serve availability queries quickly and predictably.
+**Responsibility**: Serve availability queries with predictable latency.
 
 **Key Design Decisions**:
-- Store premerged busy intervals per calendar per day/week bucket to avoid scanning instances at query time.
-- Return “unknown”/stale indicators when derived data lags beyond threshold.
+- Store pre-merged busy intervals per `(calendar_id, day)` in UTC for fast range union.
+- Include `computedAt` and `sourceVersion` so callers can detect staleness and choose to retry, accept stale, or fall back to on-demand checks.
 
-**Technology Choice**: Cassandra/ScyllaDB or DynamoDB for wide-column time-bucket data; Redis for hot ranges.
+**Technology Choice**: DynamoDB/Cassandra/Scylla for wide rows by day; Redis for hot ranges; optional compression (delta encoding).
+
+**Scaling Strategy**: Partition by `(calendar_id, bucket_day)`; cache common windows (work week); use request coalescing to avoid thundering herds on cache miss.
 
-**Scaling Strategy**: Partition by `(calendar_id, bucket_start)`; compress intervals; cache common windows (work week).
